 "description": "T22 TiDB 8.5 RU resource-group lifecycle and quota oracles. The manifest pins the frozen T22 contract: CREATE/ALTER/DROP RESOURCE GROUP reach kind=ddl with audited semantics on TiDB; authored RU_PER_SEC numeric and UNLIMITED stay distinct, bare BURSTABLE projects moderated, QUERY_LIMIT keeps typed runaway members; the resource-control capability gate tidb_enable_resource_control is a proven-refusal premise (known-OFF refuses before existence adjudication, unobserved owes unknown_resource_group_capability, never a guessed ON); the builtin default group is Reserved and its DROP is a proven refusal; unproven targets owe unknown_resource_group_state rather than a fabricated blocker or absence; proven refusals and guard no-ops suppress lifecycle notices; MySQL keeps a vendor boundary with boundary=vendor metadata for the TiDB RU forms while its own CPU VCPU family stays a parser error (T24 surface, untouched). BACKGROUND and SET RESOURCE GROUP stay bounded-outside the T22 denominator. metadata_cases encode the native probes whose oracles require the isolated TiDB 8.5 environment — none of them has run and none may be claimed as native PASS. CLI cases are provider-free offline contracts: no instance facts are observed, so each audited statement owes the capability gap plus the state gap. EXPECT FILLED: metadata_case expects completed from TiDB 8.5.0 native evidence plus the repaired contract — unvouched identities gap, never fabricate absence; a known-OFF gate refuses every lifecycle statement.",
